AcceptanceCriteria.AC-ADDITIVE-BYTE-FOOTPRINT:
`skillTextLines()` (or a co-exported pure helper documented as the
footprint API and covered by the same tests — plan may choose shape,
**meanings locked**) exposes:
- `totalBytes`: sum of UTF-8 byte lengths of the same SKILL.md files
  that contribute to `total`;
- `perSkillBytes`: per-skill-directory map of those byte lengths;
and `Object.values(perSkillBytes).reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0) === totalBytes`.
Deterministic: two calls on the same root deep-equal. **Not** a token
estimate. **Failure conditions:** only lines reported; token heuristic;
byte field counts references or plugins mirror; non-determinism;
`perSkillBytes` missing while claiming attributable footprint.

AcceptanceCriteria.AC-D14-HEAD-RED:
At red-first: `GraceCommandError` has no usable object-cause path;
`rg -n 'process\\.on\\(' src/` is empty; command.ts conversion lacks
cause. After the change: constructor + conversion sites attach cause;
process handlers exist at entry; suite proves cause identity
(`error.cause` is the original Error instance or value) and proves
JSON stdout still parses while stderr carries diagnostics. **Failure
conditions:** checks that pass on pre-change HEAD; handler untested;
cause asserted only as message equality without object identity.

VerificationIntent.ExpectedEvidence:
Integration (T2):
(F29) total still lines; totalBytes/perSkillBytes pinned; README
publishes bytes; line-neutral growth moves bytes;
(F20) exactly one function cloneXmlNode in src/, exported from xml.ts;
cursor and run-membership import it; MODULE_MAP clean;
(D14) GraceCommandError.cause is original object at command.ts and
runGraceCommand conversion; JSON mode stdout parseable envelope without
stack field; stderr carries stack/cause in text and json; process.on
handlers present under grace.ts entry path only; unhandled rejection
path exits non-zero with cause on stderr (or equivalent suite proof);
no docs/plans or archive edits; lint 0/0 **at close** only;
validate:ci green with determinism ratchet keys preserved.
